<BaseLayout
  title="The Zybach Collection (demonstration) · America's School Trust Library"
  description="An unapproved demonstration finding aid showing how a named special collection — the working archive of Dr. Zybach on the Elliott State Forest and Oregon forest history — would be described in America's School Trust Library."
  sourceId="collections-zybach"
>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-a:text-blue-700 prose-a:underline">
    <p class="unapproved-banner">
      <strong>UNAPPROVED DEMONSTRATION</strong> — This page shows how a named
      special collection would look in America's School Trust Library. It was
      prepared for Dr. Zybach's consideration and has not been approved by
      him or by the Library's board. Item lists are illustrative, drawn from his
      public work.
    </p>

    <p class="kicker">Demonstration finding aid</p>
    <h1>
      The Zybach Collection on the Elliott State Forest and Oregon Forest
      History
    </h1>

    <p>
      A named special collection is a body of work the Library accepts whole:
      kept intact, credited to its creator, and described in a published
      <em>finding aid</em> — a library's map of what a collection holds and how
      to use it. This is a demonstration of that treatment for the working
      archive of Dr. Zybach: field research, photographs, public testimony,
      maps, and writing on Oregon's forests, with the Elliott State Forest —
      school trust land for most of a century, until the State Land Board
      decoupled it from the Common School Fund in 2022 — at its center.
    </p>

    <h2>Scope</h2>

    <p>
      Materials documenting the Elliott State Forest's management, ecology, and
      public history; Oregon coastal fire history; and related Oregon forest and
      pioneer-history projects where they help readers understand the school
      trust record. The collection would be held under a deed of gift in which
      the creator retains copyright and commercial rights; the Library displays
      accepted materials free, for education and research, with attribution.
    </p>

    <p class="source-note">
      Proposed item labels below use public ORWW project titles, dates where the
      public pages give them, and links only. The linked pages remain the
      source; this demonstration does not copy the underlying materials.
    </p>

    <h2>Series (proposed)</h2>

